        <fig id="article-25803.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Snellen Chart.&#x000a0;The chart features a single large letter at the top, followed by rows of letters that become progressively smaller.&#x000a0;This evaluation tool helps determine visual acuity by identifying the smallest line of letters a person can read accurately. Public domain.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Imagen1" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-25803.s7">
        <fig id="article-25803.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Symbol-Based Visual Acuity Chart. This chart uses familiar symbols such as a house, an apple, and an umbrella instead of letters, making it suitable for children and individuals who cannot read. Public domain.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Imagen2" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-25803.s8">
        <fig id="article-25803.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Jaeger Near Vision Chart. This chart is used to evaluate near visual acuity by having patients read paragraphs of varying font sizes at a standard reading distance. Public domain.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Imagen3" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-25803.s9">
        <fig id="article-25803.image.f4" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Ishihara Color Vision Test. Example of an Ishihara test consisting of 6 plates, each composed of variably sized dots in different hues. A number embedded within each dot pattern is visible to individuals with typical red&#x02013;green color vision but is difficult or impossible to discern in those with red&#x02013;green deficiencies. The test exploits the concept of pseudoisochromaticity and remains a primary screening tool for congenital and acquired red&#x02013;green color&#x02011;vision anomalies. Public domain.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Imagen4" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
